  "harvested": "2026-10-25",
  "method": "PDF text layer (pdftotext -bbox-layout) parsed into surname/electorate label pairs by edge alignment (left-arm labels are left-justified, right-arm labels right-justified - the ring fit measures from the justified edge), including a wrap repair for the two-line 'Melbourne / Ports' electorate; every label cross-verified against (a) a macOS Vision OCR pass of the rasterised page (145/150 directly, the five edge labels - Broadbent, Fletcher, Marino, Secker, Rudd - closed by 400-dpi crops: 150/150 agreement) and (b) the in-term 43rd-Parliament roster built from this repo's 2010-election results (map/data/res-2010.json, year=2010 entries) with the in-term affiliation moves re-reflected (Slipper LNP→IND on his election as Speaker, Katter IND→KAP on his party's registration): 150/150 match for identity, with party tallies ALP 72, LP 44, LNP(Qld) 20, NP 7, CLP 1, GRN 1, KAP 1, IND 4.",
  "page": "A4 portrait, 595.276 x 841.89 pt, single page (this revision carries no alphabetical member-index page; the next revision does). The chamber is drawn with the Speaker's chair at the top (north), the table running south from it, the government on the Speaker's right (the page's LEFT), the opposition on the left (page RIGHT), the six-member crossbench around the far (south) curve.",
  "geometry": "Five concentric rows of seats about a centre near (297.6, 536); row radii 94.02, 140.17, 181.98, 221.6, 260.64 pt. Arm seats span x ~ 36..202 on the government (left) side and x ~ 361..547 on the opposition (right) side, the outer rows reaching further towards the page edges. The front row's arms extend furthest north toward the Speaker. Seat coordinates below give the surname label's north-west corner in page points, y increasing downward. The chair itself - the 'SPEAKER' label at (283.2, 208.5) - carries Peter Slipper's label ('Peter Slipper MP' / 'Fisher') printed directly above it at (275.4, 185.7).",
  "ordering": "Within each row, 'seat' numbers run from the northern (Speaker) end of the government side, around the far (south) curve, up to the northern end of the opposition side."
